{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2179-04-16 03:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hello, I'm Dr. Lee. I understand you've been having worsening abdominal pain and diarrhea. Can you tell me more about what’s been going on?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2179-04-16 03:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, thanks for coming. For about a week, my pain on the right side got worse. And my bowel movements—usually I have about 16 a day—jumped to 24, then on one day, I counted nearly 100. They’re watery."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2179-04-16 03:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That sounds really difficult. Any blood in the stool?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2179-04-16 03:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "A little—bright red, just spotting. My rectal skin feels raw from all the wiping."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2179-04-16 03:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I’m sorry you’re going through that. Any nausea or vomiting?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2179-04-16 03:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, no vomiting. But I’ve had low-grade fevers, chills, and night sweats the past couple days."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2179-04-16 03:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay. You mentioned pain—where exactly is it?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2179-04-16 03:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Dull in the upper right, but sharp and constant in the lower right and left sides. It started a few days ago."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2179-04-16 03:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Got it. We’ve reviewed your CT scan from the ER. It shows no kidney stones, which is good. But there’s thickening and inflammation in your sigmoid colon—worse than before. This suggests a flare of your Crohn’s disease."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2179-04-16 03:12:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "But I just started Tysabri four days ago. I thought that was supposed to help."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2179-04-16 03:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It should, but sometimes it takes time. In the meantime, we’re starting you on antibiotics just in case there’s an infection, and we’ll monitor your labs."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2179-04-16 03:15:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. I’ve been on so many meds before—Remicade, Cimzia—none worked well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2179-04-16 03:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I know it’s been tough. We’ve consulted GI, and they agree we should hold off on steroids tonight. We’ll wait for your stool and infection tests to come back."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2179-04-16 03:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Alright. My back’s been hurting too—same old problem, I think."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2179-04-16 03:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll address that. For now, we’re giving you IV fluids and some Dilaudid for pain. Let’s see how you do tonight."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2179-04-17 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your stool tests came back—all negative. No C. diff, no Salmonella, no Campylobacter. CMV is also negative."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2179-04-17 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So it’s not an infection?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2179-04-17 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No, it looks like this is purely a flare of your Crohn’s. We’re stopping the antibiotics. We’re also arranging an MRI for your back pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2179-04-17 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks. I’ve been nauseous—can we skip cholestyramine? I’ve tried it before and it made me sick."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2179-04-17 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Absolutely. We won’t push that. We’re discussing with your specialist about restarting steroids to control the flare."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2179-04-17 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your MRI results are back. It shows stable degenerative disc disease—moderate narrowing on the left at L5-S1. No new nerve compression or inflammation."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2179-04-17 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Same as before, then?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2179-04-17 14:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. No signs of sacroiliitis. We’ll manage your pain with Dilaudid and add tizanidine for muscle spasms. You’ll follow up with spine clinic after discharge."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2179-04-17 14:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve tried gabapentin and others—didn’t help. But tizanidine might be okay."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2179-04-17 14:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll go slow. For your Crohn’s, we’ve spoken with your specialist. Since Tysabri may take time, we’re restarting a steroid burst—prednisone—to get the flare under control."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2179-04-17 14:08:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Steroids again? I’ve had cataracts and other side effects."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2179-04-17 14:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I understand. This will be a short course, quickly tapered by your doctor. The goal is to stop the flare so you don’t end up with complications."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2179-04-17 14:12:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I trust your judgment."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2179-04-18 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. You’re looking better. Your pain is down, and your stools are less frequent—only about 8 today, and more formed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2179-04-18 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yeah, I feel like I’m turning a corner. Still tired, but the urgency is gone."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2179-04-18 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s great progress. We’ll keep you on prednisone, tizanidine, and your usual pantoprazole. We’re switching to oral Percocet for back pain as we taper IV meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2179-04-18 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I need to keep taking Percocet at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2179-04-18 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just as needed for a few weeks. We’re also sending you home with tizanidine three times a day. But no driving while on these—especially with alcohol."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2179-04-18 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. No driving. What about my Tysabri and B12 shots?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2179-04-18 09:09:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll continue both monthly. Your specialist will coordinate the next infusion."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2179-04-19 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your chest X-ray today shows no pneumonia—just a dry cough, probably from the steroids. Everything else is stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2179-04-19 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been coughing a bit, but no fever. That’s good news."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2179-04-19 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. Your Crohn’s is calming down, and your back pain is manageable. We’re planning for discharge in a couple days."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2179-04-20 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing really well. Stools are nearly normal—only 4 today. Pain is mild. We’ll finalize your discharge plan tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2179-04-20 08:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m ready to go home. What meds will I be on?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2179-04-20 08:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll take prednisone 50 mg daily—same dose—for now. Your specialist will call to taper it. Also, Percocet as needed, tizanidine three times a day, pantoprazole, Tums, B12, and Tysabri as scheduled."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2179-04-20 08:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And Seroquel? I’ve been taking that for anxiety."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2179-04-20 08:37:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ve added that too—25 mg twice daily. It’s included in your discharge meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2179-04-21 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "All set for discharge tomorrow. You’ll follow up with your GI doctor for the steroid taper and with spine clinic for your back."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2179-04-21 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I need another MRI or procedure?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2179-04-21 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not right now. The MRI was stable. If pain worsens, spine may consider intervention, but for now, conservative management."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2179-04-21 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks. I’ll keep hydrated and rest."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2179-04-22 07:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. You’re cleared to go home. Remember: no driving with Percocet and tizanidine, no alcohol, and take prednisone as directed until your doctor calls to taper it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2179-04-22 07:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. Thank you for helping me through this flare."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2179-04-22 07:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take care, and follow up as scheduled."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2179-04-16 02:40:00",
    "admission_end": "2179-04-22 11:30:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A male patient with a history of Crohn’s disease, status post subtotal colectomy and ileosigmoid anastomosis, was admitted with a one-week history of worsening right-sided abdominal pain, increased watery bowel movements up to 100 per day, and bright red blood per rectum. He had recently started Tysabri therapy. CT imaging showed worsening wall thickening and hyperemia in the sigmoid colon, consistent with active inflammatory bowel disease, with no evidence of obstruction or infection. Stool studies and CMV testing were negative. He was initially treated with antibiotics, which were discontinued after negative cultures. Due to persistent symptoms, a steroid burst with prednisone was initiated in consultation with his specialist, leading to improvement in bowel frequency and pain. His back pain was evaluated with MRI, which showed stable degenerative disc disease without new neurological compromise; he was managed with Percocet and tizanidine. He improved clinically, was transitioned to oral medications, and discharged home on a prednisone taper, continued Tysabri and B12 injections, and pain regimen with follow-up planned with GI and spine services.",
    "problems": [
      "Regional enteritis of large intestine",
      "Acquired absence of intestine (large) (small)",
      "Displacement of lumbar intervertebral disc without myelopathy",
      "Plantar fascial fibromatosis",
      "Esophageal reflux",
      "Other B-complex deficiencies",
      "Tobacco use disorder",
      "Toxic cataract",
      "Adrenal cortical steroids causing adverse effects in therapeutic use"
    ]
  }
}
